    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A plumber charges a call-out fee of \\$90 as well as \\$2 per minute while working.\n\nSuppose the plumber works for $t$ hours.\n\nWhich equation expresses the amount the plumber charges (\\$C) related to time ($t$ hours)?\n\nA. $C = 2 + 90t$\n\nB. $C = 90 + 2t$\n\nC. $C = 120 + 90t$\n\nD. $C = 90 + 120t$",
